{"term":"staple","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9307e399a5b5577946","definition":"A town containing merchants who have exclusive right, under royal authority, to purchase or produce certain goods for export; also, the body of such merchants seen as a group.","example":"The customs of Alexandria were very great, it having been the staple of the Indian trade.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"countable, historical, uncountable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:166e4a1f5eed18d1b0","definition":"Place of supply; source.","example":"Whitehall naturally became the chief staple of news. Whenever there was a rumour that anything important had happened or was about to happen, people hastened thither to obtain intelligence from the fountain head.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3f496f1d149304549f","definition":"The principal commodity produced in a town or region.","example":"The old staple of coal is a declining traffic; and what remains tends to be hauled a shorter distance, as new power stations are sited closer to coalfields.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3109392abe7e7ea0c0","definition":"A basic or essential supply.","example":"Rice is a staple in the diet of many cultures.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:284574a5c8cec7939f","definition":"A recurring topic, character, or item.","example":"Lurid stories are a staple of tabloid journalism.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:56150128bf03c12745","definition":"Short fiber, as of cotton, sheep’s wool, or the like, which can be spun into yarn or thread.","example":"Tow is flax with short staple.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:72d2d16f79cb6322f0","definition":"Unmanufactured material; raw material.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d581fde000f6d00658","definition":"To sort according to its staple.","example":"to staple cotton","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:52e708d4ff55bed52a","definition":"Relating to, or being market of staple for, commodities.","example":"a staple town","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f616a860e1087880e4","definition":"Established in commerce; occupying the markets; settled.","example":"a staple trade","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:464e24ab5cd3f01027","definition":"Fit to be sold; marketable.","example":"What needy writer would not solicit to work under such masters, who will pay us beforehand, take off as much of our ware as we please, at our own rates, and trouble not themselves to examine, either before or after they have bought it, whether it be staple, or not.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["nonstaple","staple character"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8d2fa848dd3a6ccf66","definition":"Regularly produced or manufactured in lar